# The TLS files are mandatory for the installed service. The private key must
# be unencrypted so systemd can start the monitor without an interactive prompt.
#
# If automatic discovery does not identify the router, append:
#   --gateway-address 192.168.1.1
#
# Binding to 0.0.0.0 makes the dashboard available on every IPv4 interface.
# Restrict TCP 80 and 443 to trusted management networks with firewalld or an
# upstream firewall. Port 80 serves redirects only.
#
# Full option and sampling guidance:
#   /opt/isp-loss-monitor/docs/configuration.md

ISPMON_ARGS="--listen 0.0.0.0 --port 443 --http-redirect-port 80 --csv /var/lib/isp-loss-monitor/isp-packet-loss.csv --discovery-cache /var/lib/isp-loss-monitor/discovery-cache.json --postgres-url postgresql:///isp_loss_monitor --tls-cert /etc/isp-loss-monitor/server.crt --tls-key /etc/isp-loss-monitor/server.key --terminal-mode lines"
